nd yelling at him  was not a planned or scripted bit tweets  rolled in reminding everyone that  Pinkett Smith has alopecia she first  went in public with Her diagnosis on her  Facebook live show red table talk in  2018 she said I was in the shower one  day and then just handfuls of hair just  in my hands and I was just like oh my  God am I going bald in December 2021 she  opened up about her hair loss on  Instagram telling her followers  just all of a sudden one day  look at this line right here nubbing  that Pinkett Smith is living with an  autoimmune disease makes it slightly  more understandable why her husbands did  not take kindly to rock mocking her hair  last so publicly particularly since it's  a condition with which she has clearly  struggled as seen in the live telecast  though will initially laughed at the  joke Jada was visibly unamused it's also  entirely possible that Will Smith's  anger at Chris Rock predates the 2022  Academy Awards because this isn't the  first time Ruckus publicly joked about  Pinkett Smith on stage at the Oscars in  2016 pinky Smith refused to attend the  ceremony boycotting the event due to the  awards once again having an all-white  slate of acting nominees The Smiths  weren't the only notable Hollywood  talent to ditch the ceremony either  other celebrities to skip the event  according to the independent included  Ava Duvernay Spike Lee and Ryan coogler  yet when Chris Rock took to the Oscar  stage as that Year's host it was Pinkett  Smith he chose as his Target he implied  she wasn't invited at all saying saying  Jada said she's not coming I was like  isn't she on a TV show at the time  Pinker Smith publicly dismissed Rock's  commentary but she and her husband's  private feelings about the matter may  have been different from what she said  publicly whether it was a long-standing  bad blood or a knee-jerk reaction to a  joke Will Smith's actions certainly took  the Academy Awards to a strange place  that will not be forgotten 